{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":24,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.det_eq_one_at_octahedron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.det_eq_one_at_octahedron","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronConcavity.lean#L241-L249","doc":"The determinant is `1` at the octahedral point — the potentially degenerate\none — so negative definiteness is not lost there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.regularOctahedron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.regularOctahedron","kind":"def","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronConcavity.lean#L226-L239","doc":"The regular ideal OCTAHEDRON triple — L6a4's unique symmetric point\n(`L6a4AngleStructure.unique_symmetric_point`), in radians.\n\nThis is the case worth having: `cot(π/2) = 0`, so the Hessian's off-diagonal\nvanishes and the matrix *looks* degenerate. It is not — `hessian_det_eq_one`\ngives determinant exactly `1` here too. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.regularTetrahedron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.regularTetrahedron","kind":"def","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronConcavity.lean#L215-L224","doc":"The regular ideal TETRAHEDRON triple — m004's Casson-Rivin optimum\n(`M004AngleStructure.regular_unique_on_fixed_locus`), in radians. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.hessian_det_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.hessian_det_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronConcavity.lean#L199-L207","doc":"The determinant, isolated: it is exactly `1` everywhere on the simplex — not\nmerely positive.  Recorded separately because the exactness is the surprising\npart and is what keeps the octahedral point non-degenerate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.hessian_neg_definite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.hessian_neg_definite","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronConcavity.lean#L178-L197","doc":"**The Hessian of the ideal-tetrahedron volume is negative definite.**\n\nEntries `A = -(cot α + cot γ)`, `B = -cot γ`, `C = -(cot β + cot γ)`.  The proof\nis the two identities: `A < 0` by `cot_add_cot_pos`, and `A·C - B² = 1` by\n`cot_cyclic_sum_eq_one`.\n\nHolds at every interior point of the simplex, the regular octahedral triple\n`(π/4, π/4, π/2)` included — there `cot γ = 0` and the matrix looks degenerate,\nbut the determinant is still exactly `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.quadratic_neg_of_lead_neg_of_det_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.quadratic_neg_of_lead_neg_of_det_pos","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronConcavity.lean#L154-L176","doc":"A symmetric `2x2` form with negative leading entry and positive determinant\nis negative definite.  Completing the square: `A·Q = (A x + B y)² + (AC - B²) y²`,\nand `A < 0` flips it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.cot_add_cot_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.cot_add_cot_pos","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronConcavity.lean#L146-L150","doc":"Hence `cot α + cot γ > 0`, so the Hessian's diagonal entries are negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.cot_add_cot_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.cot_add_cot_eq","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronConcavity.lean#L134-L144","doc":"**`cot α + cot γ = sin β / (sin α sin γ)`.**  Immediate from the sine\naddition formula, since `α + γ = π - β`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.cot_cyclic_sum_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.cot_cyclic_sum_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronConcavity.lean#L112-L130","doc":"**`cot α cot β + cot β cot γ + cot γ cot α = 1` for `α + β + γ = π`.**\n\nThis is what makes `det H = 1` exactly, at every interior point.  Proved by\nclearing denominators onto the sine addition formula: with\n`sin(α+β) = sin γ` and `cos(α+β) = -cos γ`, the numerator collapses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.sin_γ_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.sin_γ_pos","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronConcavity.lean#L106-L106","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.sin_β_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.sin_β_pos","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronConcavity.lean#L105-L105","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.sin_α_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.sin_α_pos","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronConcavity.lean#L103-L104","doc":"Every angle has strictly positive sine — the workhorse. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.γ_lt_pi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.γ_lt_pi","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronConcavity.lean#L101-L101","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.β_lt_pi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.β_lt_pi","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronConcavity.lean#L100-L100","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.α_lt_pi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.α_lt_pi","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronConcavity.lean#L99-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.sum","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronConcavity.lean#L93-L93","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.hγ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.hγ","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronConcavity.lean#L92-L92","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.hβ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.hβ","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronConcavity.lean#L91-L91","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.hα","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.hα","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronConcavity.lean#L90-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.γ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.γ","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronConcavity.lean#L89-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.β","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.β","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronConcavity.lean#L88-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.α","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.α","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronConcavity.lean#L87-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.mk","kind":"ctor","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronConcavity.lean#L86-L86","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple","kind":"structure","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronConcavity.lean#L84-L93","doc":"The dihedral-angle triple of an ideal tetrahedron: three positive angles\nsumming to `π`.  (Positivity plus the sum forces each to lie in `(0, π)`.) ","signatureChunk":0}]}